--- body ---
## Context

Second round of live findings, testing v0.3.17 (ticket 0748's own fixes)
right after install. Two of these are correctness bugs the author's own
observation exposed, not cosmetic ones.

## Findings and fixes

1. **The progress bar never reached completion after switching off
   mid-extraction, contradicting the disclosure's own "one already being
   processed still finishes."** Root cause, in two parts:
   - `scheduler.js`'s `publish()` gated `host.changed(state)` — the only
     thing that repaints the dialog outside the periodic pulse the switch
     already tears down — on `state.enabled`. So a job that kept genuinely
     running never got shown doing so.
   - Deeper: once a document was already handed to the native worker, several
     `if (!state.enabled) break/return` checks skipped its own settlement
     entirely — no `inspect()`, no `state.completed++`, no census update, on
     success OR failure. The native pack really did persist (DECISIONS.md,
     2026-09-05: "C'est plutot bien qu'il finisse le travail en cours" /
     "may finish and persist its native pack"), but the sitter's own
     bookkeeping silently dropped it, leaving the census wrong until some
     later sweep happened to notice.

   Fixed by removing the `enabled` gate from `publish()` and from every
   check downstream of a document already being admitted — the OUTER loops
   (census walk, next-candidate admission) still gate on `enabled`
   unconditionally, so no new document is ever admitted while off; only the
   one already in flight is now fully seen through to its real outcome.

2. **The census-account and native-fulltext tables were padded `<pre>` text,
   which does not align in the dialog's own proportional UI font
   (`font: inherit`)** — ticket 0748's own alignment fix had shipped and
   still didn't align, since a `<pre>` reflows to whatever font the
   surrounding window uses, not necessarily a monospace one. Rebuilt both as
   real `<table>` elements with `text-align: right` on the count cell, which
   aligns in any font.

3. **A single, routine extraction failure surfaced as a top-of-window
   "Error:" banner**, alongside its own row in the census account
   ("Extraction failed this session") — the same fact stated twice, one of
   them reading as an unqualified alarm. Moved into Technical diagnostics,
   where a reader opens specifically for raw detail, and reworded ("Last
   extraction problem") so it no longer overclaims for one failed attachment
   among possibly thousands.

4. **"Created this session: {count}" named no subject.** Reworded to
   "Attachments indexed this session: {count}".

5. **The on/off button wrapped onto two lines at some dialog widths, turning
   it into a square, one line at others.** `element()`'s default styling
   (written for the prose blocks) carries `white-space: pre-wrap`, which the
   button inherited along with everything else built through that helper.
   The button now overrides it to a single line (`white-space: nowrap;
   flex-shrink: 0`); the state text beside it gets `min-width: 0` so it is
   the one that shrinks and wraps in a narrow window, not the control.

## Test

- `tests/sdt_sitter_scheduler.mjs`: the two tests pinning "no UI callback
  while disabled" reworded to assert the opposite, with the new contract
  spelled out (a scheduler-level `host.changed` unconditional on `enabled`;
  what actually gates a redraw in production is `render()`'s own `alive`
  check, which this fixture does not model).
- `tests/sdt_sitter_bootstrap.mjs`: a real dialog opened, a job switched off
  mid-extraction, and both `state.completed` and the document-status text
  asserted to reach real completion — the integration-level proof the
  scheduler-level test alone cannot give. Verified red against the
  pre-fix `scheduler.js` via `git stash`.
- `tests/sdt_sitter_dialog.mjs`: the census-account test rewritten against
  the `<table>` DOM (row/cell lookups, not text-line splitting); the
  fulltext-stats test likewise; a new test for the button's nowrap/min-width
  declarations; a new test for the error line's disclosure and wording.
  Verified red against the pre-fix `bootstrap.js` via `git stash`.
- `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py`: two `_site` anchors updated to the code's new
  shape (the named `diagnosticsHead` constant is gone; the assignment and the
  account composer's call site moved).

## Verification

- [x] All four `.mjs` suites pass
- [x] `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py`, `tests/test_sitter_host_apis.py` pass
- [x] `make check-fast` — 1311 passed, 1 pre-existing environmental failure
      (podman rootless-container store, unrelated, documented this session)
- [x] Manifest/update.json bumped 0.3.17 -> 0.3.18, version guard clean
- [x] Both scheduler-level behavior changes verified with a positive control
      (reddened against the pre-fix code via `git stash`)

## Exit criteria

A document already handed to the native worker always reaches its real
outcome in the census, on/off notwithstanding, and an open dialog shows that
happening. The two tabular displays align in any font. The Error line and
its wording no longer overclaim. The switch button never wraps.
